<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dihqan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The dihqans were the Persian landed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a> of the Sasanian era, who managed villages and collected taxes. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> relied on them as local intermediaries for tax collection and administration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, preserving much of the earlier fiscal system under Muslim rule.</p></div>
